 "notes": "Approximate digitization; not supplied or endorsed by Eastman Kodak Company. Sensitometry x = (log H - Log H Ref) / log10(2), Log H Ref -0.893 lux-seconds derived from the datasheet's grey-card red density aim (see below); density is Status M including base, made monotone by running maximum. Spectral sensitivity kept only where the curve is drawn on the chart; wavelengths where a curve is not drawn are omitted. Individual dye curves not published; dye_density holds only the published midscale neutral and minimum density curves. Characteristic curves: Exposure Daylight, Process C-41, Densitometry Status M; the chart prints no Log H Ref, so the grey reference (Log H Ref -0.893) is the log H where the red Status M curve reaches 1.13, the middle of the 1.03-1.23 red density the datasheet's 'Judging Negative Exposure' text gives for a KODAK Gray Card (gray side) in a normally exposed negative (aim band log H -1.069 to -0.715). Log-exposure labels use bar notation (3-bar.0 = -3.0), axes calibrated from the drawn tick marks (log H -3.0 and 0.0; density 1.0 and 3.0), which put density 0.0 on the drawn frame bottom. Spectral sensitivity: effective exposure 1/50 s, Process C-41, Status M, density 0.2 above D-min; this chart's log-sensitivity axis runs 0.0 to 4.0, calibrated from the 1.0 and 3.0 grid lines. Spectral dye density: typical densities for a midscale neutral subject and D-min, Process C-41. Print Grain Index table as published (page 4): only the 24 x 36 mm (135) negative size is published, no print sizes in cm beyond the 10.2 x 15.2, 20.3 x 25.4 and 40.6 x 50.8 cm equivalents. No MTF chart is published.",
